.TITLE "pbcopy"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Copies data from standard input to the clipboard. It allows you to programmatically capture command output and store it in the system __pasteboard__ for use in other applications.

.DIV "TLDR"
**echo "text" | pbcopy**
Copies the output of a command or a string to the clipboard.
> __"text"__ the input data

**pbcopy < file.txt**
Copies the entire contents of a text file to the clipboard.
> __<__ input redirection | __file.txt__ the source file

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __pbcopy__ is a highly efficient way to handle long strings like __SSH keys__ or __UUIDs__ without manual selection. Combine it with __pbpaste__ to complete the workflow.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:pbpaste**

